Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.66,0:00:07.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Sure enough, there aren't any more books written about the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.98,0:00:10.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What that minister had was a fake,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.70,0:00:13.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and once again, we don't have any other leads.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.42,0:00:16.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How about we head \Nback to Central, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.19,0:00:17.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.18,0:00:19.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.49,0:00:22.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"An Introduction to Alchemy." \NThis sure takes me back.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.50,0:00:24.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh, it does?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.45,0:00:40.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.51,0:00:42.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,this is boring!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.96,0:00:44.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Hold on, just a little longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.44,0:00:46.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}All right, done!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.50,0:00:47.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Watch this, Winry!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.88,0:00:50.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You said you were giving me a present.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.04,0:00:54.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And we're making your present right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.96,0:01:46.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was our very first transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.52,0:01:52.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.25,0:01:57.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.52,0:02:02.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's\NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.26,0:02:08.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.32,0:04:01.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry, you were wrong to do that \Nafter those two went to all that trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.62,0:04:07.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right. Both Edward-chan and Alphonse-chan were doing it for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.20,0:04:09.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm really sorry about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.94,0:04:12.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter how much they learn,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.72,0:04:16.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the usual person gives up \Nsomewhere along the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.15,0:04:19.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, those boys are already magnificent alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.18,0:04:25.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But those boys shouldn't know anything about alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.78,0:04:29.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They are {\i1}his{\i0} sons after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.06,0:04:43.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So when did your dad \Nteach you about alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.30,0:04:45.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could we learn anything from someone who isn't ever around?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.52,0:04:47.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was written in that book.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.88,0:04:50.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can understand something as difficult as this?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.00,0:04:51.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,More or less.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.14,0:04:53.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did we do anything wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.77,0:04:58.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, you did outstanding! \NI think I'll brag to everyone about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.67,0:05:04.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be sure to put the books back where you find them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.38,0:05:08.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once Dad comes home, \Nmake sure to thank him. And lastly,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.07,0:05:09.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,do not open that door.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.83,0:05:11.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Understood!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.56,0:05:12.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here they are!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.37,0:05:25.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad departed without telling anyone where he was going,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.72,0:05:28.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so Mom started staring off into the distance a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.22,0:05:32.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But still, once we began practicing alchemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.80,0:05:35.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,she would smile at us \Nmore frequently.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.23,0:05:38.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mother was praising us.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.23,0:05:41.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We competed with each other \Nas we became absorbed in alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.24,0:05:47.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.20,0:05:49.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.36,0:05:51.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Look, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.45,0:05:52.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}See?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.24,0:05:52.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, my!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.87,0:05:55.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother made it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.04,0:05:56.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can still only do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.87,0:05:59.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Incredible, both of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.04,0:06:01.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You certainly are his children!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.85,0:06:04.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would Father commend us too?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.76,0:06:08.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.12,0:06:09.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once he comes home, \NI'm sure he will.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.86,0:06:14.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going over to Winry's!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.20,0:06:15.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.94,0:06:27.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.38,0:06:30.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,do you hate Father?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.24,0:06:32.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't say I hate him...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.00,0:06:34.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just don't remember him too well.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.76,0:06:41.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whenever anyone talks about him, Mom makes a strange face.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.86,0:06:43.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what I don't like.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.66,0:06:45.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,S-Sorry...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.53,0:06:53.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go over to Winry's!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.63,0:07:02.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.05,0:07:03.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just like I told you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.61,0:07:06.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My mom and dad are dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.11,0:07:12.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,B-But your folks are doctors, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.12,0:07:15.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right. That's why they went to the war in Ishbal,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.81,0:07:17.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and now they're dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.05,0:07:22.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,W-Winry,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.47,0:07:24.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,our father is...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.60,0:07:26.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,kind of in the same situation...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.32,0:07:28.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not the same!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.13,0:07:31.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're dead, that means \Nyou can never come back again!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.10,0:07:35.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's {\i1}not{\i0} as though you can't ever come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.34,0:07:38.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I read so in a book.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.17,0:07:41.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's this artificial person thing, \Ncalled a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.28,0:07:43.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sounds sort of like a doll that doesn't have a mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.11,0:07:46.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But with alchemy, \Nyour folks could probably be—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.81,0:07:47.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop right there!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.31,0:07:50.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is something \Nwhich is not allowed!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.24,0:07:54.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemy is not all-powerful.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.13,0:07:57.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why we Automail \Nengineers exist, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.40,0:08:00.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dirty old hag...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.90,0:08:11.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I feel sorry for Winry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.20,0:08:31.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter with you two?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.22,0:08:35.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter, Edward? You're such a big boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.70,0:08:37.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This looks funny, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.34,0:08:50.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, you're so slow!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.95,0:09:00.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom, sorry we're late!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.06,0:09:09.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.84,0:09:11.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.15,0:09:19.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She hasn't been sick since just today or yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.60,0:09:23.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She must've been suffering \Nfrom this illness for years now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.14,0:09:28.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Honey...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.86,0:09:34.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These here are letters \Nthat came for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.93,0:09:38.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we send a letter to \Neach one of them...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.02,0:09:42.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone will know where he is and tell him to come home?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.30,0:09:46.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want him to come home! \NBut we don't have any choice! Damn!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.18,0:09:52.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your dad...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.94,0:09:55.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,left us this money.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.15,0:09:58.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I haven't touched it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.23,0:09:59.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Use that,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.24,0:10:01.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the two of you \Ntake care of each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.22,0:10:04.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about, Mom?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.90,0:10:07.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would you transmute something for me...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.85,0:10:09.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.03,0:10:11.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.77,0:10:13.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A corsage would be nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.80,0:10:17.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He... always...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.38,0:10:21.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,made them... for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.70,0:10:34.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The reason Mom was so thrilled to see us practicing alchemy
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.44,0:10:36.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was that it reminded her of Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.60,0:10:39.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what we finally realized.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.88,0:10:50.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.82,0:10:52.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm hungry.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.25,0:10:55.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm cold as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.92,0:10:59.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.17,0:11:00.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.98,0:11:03.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.08,0:11:05.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,bring Mom back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.12,0:11:17.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Look, here in his notes!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.98,0:11:19.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't understand it all,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.48,0:11:21.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but something about human transmutation is written here!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.83,0:11:24.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we can decipher this...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.07,0:11:28.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it's written here that human transmutation is forbidden.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.58,0:11:31.94,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,If dead people can come back to life, \Nthen of course it would make anyone happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.94,0:11:34.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nobody has succeeded, \Nand they're all frustrated,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.16,0:11:36.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so the grown-ups have just prohibited it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.70,0:11:40.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, if you, me, and Mom can all live happily together again,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.02,0:11:42.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then Mom would be thrilled!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.59,0:11:45.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, maybe we should \Nask Dad about this first...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.90,0:11:48.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's his fault that Mom died!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.51,0:11:51.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom was always waiting for him,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.18,0:11:54.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and he didn't even \Ncome home for her funeral!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.86,0:11:58.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If this is something that he \Ncouldn't do, then {\i1}we'll{\i0} do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.32,0:12:00.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We're{\i0} gonna do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.02,0:12:07.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We found ourselves a teacher \Nand learned alchemy from the beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.87,0:12:09.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then, one day...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.90,0:12:14.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Water, 35 liters;
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.88,0:12:18.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,carbon, 20 kilograms; ammonia, 4 liters;
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.88,0:12:21.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,lime, 1.5 kilograms...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.10,0:12:22.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Phosphorus, 800 grams;
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.88,0:12:26.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,salt, 250 grams; saltpeter, 100 grams;
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.30,0:12:29.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,fluorine, 7.5 grams;
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.75,0:12:32.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,iron, 5 grams; silicon, 3 grams...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.51,0:12:36.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These are the elements that comprise an adult human—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.85,0:12:38.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the structural formula.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.18,0:12:41.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By including a soul in this,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.42,0:12:46.41,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,we should be able to call Mom's spirit back and connect it with her body once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.68,0:12:48.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, are you sure we should?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.75,0:12:50.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After we've come this far, Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.82,0:12:54.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But still, alchemy is about \Nequivalent exchange, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.53,0:12:57.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've got the ingredients for the body,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.12,0:13:00.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but what do we exchange for Mom's spirit?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.36,0:13:01.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't worry, just stick out your finger.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.69,0:13:11.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Information...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.18,0:13:13.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,about the soul...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.30,0:13:18.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.56,0:13:20.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's do it, Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.18,0:13:33.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The village of Resembool...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.60,0:13:58.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, something's not right here!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.75,0:14:05.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.00,0:14:12.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.66,0:14:13.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.83,0:14:19.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.82,0:14:23.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.27,0:14:27.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The last thing I saw
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.42,0:14:31.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was the sight of Brother's left leg \Nbeing broken down and disappearing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.90,0:14:33.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.24,0:14:46.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.10,0:14:56.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.40,0:14:57.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.80,0:15:02.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, what happened to me? And...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.75,0:15:04.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,your arm...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.34,0:15:08.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With just my right arm,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.34,0:15:14.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was only able to bond your spirit to the armor that was sitting over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.10,0:15:16.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.97,0:15:21.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what about Mom?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.05,0:15:21.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It wasn't...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.66,0:15:24.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,human.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.74,0:15:30.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That can't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.20,0:15:34.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How come? Brother, your theories should have been perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.77,0:15:37.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My theories weren't what was wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.20,0:15:40.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What was wrong...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.95,0:15:42.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was us.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.58,0:15:44.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Grandma!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.50,0:15:46.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.28,0:15:50.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Help my brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.47,0:15:52.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.95,0:15:54.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is that you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.10,0:16:01.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys are back from your training?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.10,0:16:02.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then, why?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.78,0:16:07.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you were thinking of creating your mom.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.30,0:16:13.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it. That was the light \Nof human transmutation, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.47,0:16:17.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've never seen such a furious reaction in a transmutation before.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.52,0:16:19.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pardon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.95,0:16:22.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A State Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.93,0:16:25.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What business does \Nthe military have here?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.03,0:16:28.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As you can see, these boys \Nhave suffered grave injuries.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.37,0:16:31.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This letter came my way.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.30,0:16:34.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's one that Brother sent to Dad's acquaintances!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.13,0:16:39.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've been searching for your father, Hohenheim, for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.61,0:16:42.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We still don't know \Nwhere their father is.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.53,0:16:44.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are hurt people here. Go away.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.70,0:16:48.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they performed human transmutation
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.24,0:16:50.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and escaped with their lives,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.20,0:16:53.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then I am more interested in them \Nthan in their father.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.97,0:16:56.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They could make fine State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.32,0:16:59.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This boy hasn't done anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.83,0:17:02.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go away, we have things to do here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.73,0:17:07.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am State Alchemist \NLt. Col. Roy Mustang.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.52,0:17:10.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come pay a visit to Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.05,0:17:41.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, good morning, Winry.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.72,0:17:45.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al! You're awake?! \NI-I'm sorry, I was just...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.50,0:17:52.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Grandma, in the house, there's some money...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.84,0:17:55.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You dummy, don't be worried over something as trivial as that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.66,0:17:57.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not what I meant.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.30,0:18:00.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Use that money and fix me up \Nwith some Automail.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.10,0:18:05.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to go see that Roy guy from earlier
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.21,0:18:07.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and become a State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.47,0:18:10.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll need the freedom of my own arms and legs to do so, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.52,0:18:13.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean, you were listening?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.69,0:18:17.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard about them from my teacher. If I become a State Alchemist,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.32,0:18:20.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll be able to read valuable documents that the state is in charge of.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.26,0:18:23.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll also be provided an allowance \Nand allowed to do research on my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.40,0:18:28.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more, that watch \Ncan amplify an alchemist's power.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.02,0:18:32.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Didn't your teacher tell you this?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.05,0:18:36.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once war breaks out, \Nyou will be brought into it,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.16,0:18:42.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and if ordered, use your alchemy to \Ntake lives for the good of the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.38,0:18:45.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the war that claimed \Nmy own sons' lives,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.78,0:18:48.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there were State Alchemists involved.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.87,0:18:52.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't care if I have to become \Na dog of the military or whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.03,0:18:54.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is something that I have to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.80,0:18:57.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed, are you still at it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.82,0:19:04.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just bear with us. This is the highest-quality stuff I can make!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.40,0:19:09.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're okay! Don't come in!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.71,0:19:11.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm surprised.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.65,0:19:16.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even adults scream at the pain of attaching each nerve to the mechanisms.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.12,0:19:19.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This pain is nothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.45,0:19:21.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,compared to his.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.34,0:19:37.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been a while. \NShall we go at it,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.70,0:19:39.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.34,0:19:42.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"To train the mind, \None must train the body."
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.50,0:19:45.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what Teacher said.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.45,0:19:48.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But, Al, are you going to be able to handle it in that body?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.38,0:19:50.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not going to lose \Nto some Automail!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.22,0:20:11.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, are you serious about becoming a State Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.38,0:20:15.82,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,I don't know whether or not I can become one, \Nbut I am going to go see that Roy guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.82,0:20:17.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.18,0:20:18.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've made up my mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.65,0:20:19.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well then, I'll become one!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.70,0:20:22.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.27,0:20:26.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, are you still \Nplanning to transmute Mom?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.37,0:20:32.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You said at the time that we were wrong to do so, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.57,0:20:37.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll become a State Alchemist,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.50,0:20:44.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and then I'll find a way to \Nget your arm and leg back.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.32,0:20:47.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't have to worry about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.80,0:20:49.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it's my fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.96,0:20:53.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I had objected, \Nyou wouldn't have lost your leg!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.20,0:20:58.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then you lost your arm in order to bond my spirit...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.40,0:21:05.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What about you? What are you supposed to do with that body?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.66,0:21:09.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.01,0:21:12.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to go find a way \Nto get you back to normal.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.62,0:21:15.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You won't try anything with Mom, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.94,0:21:21.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's likely that there isn't anything in the world
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.28,0:21:23.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that we can exchange \Nequivalently for Mom's life.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.48,0:21:25.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And besides...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.74,0:21:27.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want to lose you too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.52,0:21:32.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, \NI'm going with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.45,0:21:33.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But why?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.50,0:21:36.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, you slack off too quickly! If I'm not around...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.70,0:21:38.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what you're getting at?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.64,0:21:40.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And I...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.73,0:21:42.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,don't ever want us \Nto get separated again.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.86,0:22:01.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even though they \Nwere our own bodies,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.96,0:22:06.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we would still be seeking to perform a forbidden human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.70,0:22:07.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If unsuccessful,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.40,0:22:10.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,this time we would probably \Ndisappear from this world for good.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.94,0:22:15.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There would be no telling what further punishment we would receive.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.82,0:22:18.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There could be no \Nturning back for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.00,0:22:22.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}And so, on the day \Nwe left on our journey,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.90,0:22:24.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}we burned down our house.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.05,0:23:40.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.57,0:23:42.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 4: "Transmutation of Love"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.98,0:23:47.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When a doll takes on life, a man learns of his own foolishness.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.28,0:23:51.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet he'll do it again \Nif he can transmute love.
